config WTK_DA218B
	bool "MiraMEMS DA218-B (mir3da) for MediaTek package (Doogee S88 Pro, from the disassembly)"
	default n
	help
	  MiraMEMS DA218-B accelerometer ("mir3da" in the factory symbols) of the
	  Doogee S88 Pro, reconstructed by reading the disassembled factory
	  kernel.  The factory config turns it on (CONFIG_WTK_DA218B=y, line 1557
	  of e977_dg_m13_71_q0.config); no public tree has the source -- neither
	  ALPS nor the .186 branch.

	  Two translation units: mir3da_cust.c (37 functions out of 37) and
	  mir3da_core.c (19 of the core block's 29 functions).  The 19 are the
	  transitive closure of what the link needs: the 9 boundary ones declared
	  in mir3da_core.h, the 6 those call (mir3da_read_raw_data,
	  mir3da_temp_calibrate, mir3da_read_offset, mir3da_parse_chip_info,
	  mir3da_module_detect, squareRoot) and the 4 pointed at by the chip
	  descriptor table.  The 10 left out are globals no other kernel object
	  calls: the list, with the reason, is in the header of mir3da_core.c, §1.
